1
00:00:10,207 --> 00:00:11,583
(Sun Honglei)

2
00:00:11,967 --> 00:00:13,049
(Li Naiwen)

3
00:00:14,943 --> 00:00:16,511
(Guo Jingfei)

4
00:00:17,047 --> 00:00:19,077
(Liu Yuning)

5
00:00:19,295 --> 00:00:21,130
(Gong Jun)

6
00:00:22,241 --> 00:00:23,053
(Chen Xingxu)

7
00:00:23,705 --> 00:00:26,303
(Wang Yuwen)

8
00:00:26,596 --> 00:00:28,671
(Lin Yi)

9
00:00:31,967 --> 00:00:34,542
=Wow The World S2 Extra Episode=

10
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,200
Everyone just had

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,320
an intense Lemon Queen Chase.

12
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,960
Next, we will have a bonus round.

13
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,160
I think we should play

14
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:43,720
a psychological mind game.

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,600
A verbal deduction game, right?

16
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,680
Well, actually, back there,

17
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:49,320
it felt like
a Western cowboy duel scene,

18
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,400
with one person on each side,

19
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,000
full of momentum.

20
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:51,400
Just like that.

21
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,200
(You know what I mean?)
Sounds good?

22
00:00:52,807 --> 00:00:54,079
(Thinking)

23
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,800
(Locking on target)
We stand together and ask, "Is it you?"

24
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:56,560
Right.

25
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,160
Let's think about the rules
for verbal deduction.

26
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:58,760
Just like the previous rules.

27
00:00:58,760 --> 00:00:59,440
The same rules.

28
00:00:59,440 --> 00:01:01,160
We stand in two rows
for verbal deduction

29
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:02,080
and strike this pose.

30
00:01:02,223 --> 00:01:03,740
(A true Western cowboy)

31
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:09,040
What we're playing is...

32
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:09,920
Verbal deduction.

33
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,360
Just like Western cowboys'

34
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:12,520
duel.

35
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:14,160
Each side sends one member.

36
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,520
They decide whether to pop
each other's balloons.

37
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:16,280
(Keep it simple)
How about that?

38
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:18,680
What if we win again this round?

39
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,280
(Seeking revenge)
That's basically impossible.

40
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:24,120
That's presumptuous.

41
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:26,520
Later, edit in what Yuning said to us

42
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:27,760
right before we left,

43
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,680
when we were just about to set off.

44
00:01:29,689 --> 00:01:30,512
(Wow The World S2 Episode 4 Part 2)
Go for it, guys.

45
00:01:30,512 --> 00:01:31,606
(Smug)
Don't lose too quickly.

46
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,480
Don't lose too quickly.

47
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:35,720
Don't lose too quickly.

48
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:40,080
We don't feel pressure at all.

49
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,600
We don't feel pressure at all.

50
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:43,640
Okay, I've caught my breath.

51
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:44,280
I'll run.

52
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:47,720
Okay, come on.

53
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:49,920
Come on.

54
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,160
Yuning.

55
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,120
Yuning.

56
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,280
Tie your shoelaces first.

57
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,480
Come on.

58
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:05,120
(Brothers lead their sister to victory)
We just wanted Zhou Ye to experience it.

59
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,520
We three Ferraris,

60
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,039
even when old,

61
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:09,800
(Old Ferraris are still Ferraris)
are still pretty good.

62
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:15,160
So awesome.

63
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:17,080
Do you need us to go easy on you?

64
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:17,680
Sure.

65
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:18,200
Yes.

66
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:19,120
Yes, very much so.

67
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,000
(Begging for mercy)
We're getting old.

68
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:20,680
Record this.

69
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:22,440
If we lose, we'll say we let them win.

70
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,840
Thanks, Yuning, for going easy on us.

71
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:24,400
Alright.

72
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:26,240
Don't lose too quickly.

73
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,480
Yuning, I love shooting shows
with you so much.

74
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,080
Really?

75
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:33,440
You are truly amazing.

76
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,120
Handsome and smart.

77
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:36,200
And talented too.

78
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:36,920
That's me.

79
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,160
I'm the queen.

80
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,680
Stop. Don't praise him too much.

81
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:41,200
Or he might pop it.

82
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:41,880
I'll pop it myself.

83
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:42,240
I will.

84
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:43,760
Well, you have to keep praising him,

85
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:45,080
or he'll snap out of it, you know?

86
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,600
(Predicting Yuning's reaction)
Here, pop it.

87
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:49,880
No, it's really not me.

88
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,280
And if you praise him again...

89
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,120
Fine, here you go.

90
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:55,640
Alright, let's go.

91
00:02:55,960 --> 00:02:56,600
Come on.

92
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:57,880
So we should continue
our discussion, right?

93
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:58,800
Back to our spawn point.

94
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,200
This time,

95
00:03:01,200 --> 00:03:02,440
let's just point, okay?

96
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,160
Who?

97
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,440
I think...

98
00:03:05,856 --> 00:03:06,320
(Picking Sun Honglei as the queen)

99
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,800
They probably

100
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,520
won't expect him.

101
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,400
I think they might.

102
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:13,200
Probably not.

103
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,640
(Who dares touch Cool Lei?)
They won't dare touch him.

104
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,320
So what if we use our seniority?

105
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:18,080
That's our advantage.

106
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:18,400
Right.

107
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,040
So what if we're shameless?

108
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:22,840
A disadvantage...

109
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:24,440
A disadvantage can be turned
into an advantage.

110
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,240
Right.

111
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,880
Jingfei, I think it should be you.

112
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,040
(Creating confusion)
Stop yelling, in case they hear.

113
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,080
Fine, then it's me.

114
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,280
Jingfei.

115
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:33,480
So it's Jingfei, right?

116
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:33,760
Okay.

117
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:34,480
(Agreement reached)
Okay.

118
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:35,040
(Lemon Queen decided: Sun Honglei)
Okay.

119
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,240
No one's listening, really.

120
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,800
They'll never guess it.

121
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:38,800
Just in case, you know?

122
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,880
Walls have ears.

123
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:40,720
You never know.

124
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,760
What if he's

125
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,400
Xingxu in disguise?

126
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,920
(Dare to answer if I call you?)
Xingxu, drop the disguise.

127
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,400
Alright.

128
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,400
It's not him.

129
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:51,000
Back to square one.

130
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,520
Back to the loser spawn point.

131
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:54,520
We get back up where we fell.

132
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,320
Okay, we have a bench here
to sit for a bit.

133
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,320
What's the plan?

134
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:00,320
I think this round it's Ye or Fei.

135
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,400
I think it's still Naiwen.

136
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,520
Maybe, who knows.

137
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:04,120
But Fei was really hyped up,

138
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,320
so he might volunteer.

139
00:04:05,535 --> 00:04:06,967
(You all guessed wrong)

140
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:08,200
Then who is our queen?

141
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:09,680
You.

142
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:11,760
(Me? Just like that?)
Is it decided?

143
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,640
It'll work. I think it'll work.

144
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:14,458
How about you guys?

145
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:17,800
(On high alert)
They're here.

146
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,440
(Enemies have arrived)
This place is great for a showdown.

147
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,320
Right?

148
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:22,520
Yeah, it has good depth.

149
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,680
We haven't figured it out yet.

150
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:25,920
What's wrong? Out of stamina,

151
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:26,960
and out of brainpower too?

152
00:04:26,960 --> 00:04:28,520
Our brains are totally fried right now.

153
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:29,840
We've been dazed by failure.

154
00:04:29,966 --> 00:04:31,463
(Why don't I believe that at all?)

155
00:04:31,537 --> 00:04:32,080
(One starts)

156
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,200
We're done for.

157
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,440
What do we do?

158
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,920
(The other follows)
We've been completely crushed.

159
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:38,680
We have no confidence left.

160
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:39,840
Come on.

161
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,360
(Can't wait)
Let's head into town

162
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,520
and have a showdown.

163
00:04:42,840 --> 00:04:44,040
We haven't decided yet.

164
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,080
Are we having the showdown right here?

165
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,320
This round is very important to us.

166
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,520
It's a battle for dignity.

167
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:48,760
We'll help you decide.

168
00:04:50,850 --> 00:04:51,640
(If one person fails, ask another)

169
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,040
Who are you picking?

170
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:55,720
(No way to bait me)
I can't tell you who it is.

171
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:57,040
(Sending guests away)
Go rest for a bit.

172
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:57,720
So you can...

173
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,040
Your stamina is clearly lacking.

174
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:01,200
Get some good rest.

175
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,760
They're talking so tough.

176
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:06,240
If we can't win the game,

177
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:08,040
(At least talk trash)
can't we at least talk some trash?

178
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:09,160
Let's go.

179
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:11,400
Let's look at the view.

180
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,240
Look at the view.

181
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:13,640
Let's head over there.

182
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:14,440
It's pretty nice there.

183
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:17,120
You can take some photos and check in.

184
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:17,825
(Just what I had in mind)

185
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:18,640
Look.

186
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:19,840
Look how relaxed we are,

187
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:21,400
basking in the sunset.

188
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,120
It's so cozy.

189
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,240
Let's take some nice photos.

190
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,040
(Granting your wish)
Come on.

191
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:26,960
We should do this.

192
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,800
Let it float.

193
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:29,400
(Elderly people's photo pose 1:
Holding scarf high overhead)

194
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:30,000
Hurry.

195
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:30,720
Let's do it together.

196
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:31,440
I'll do this.

197
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,000
Right, come on.

198
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:32,560
I'll do this.

199
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:34,400
Ready? Go.

200
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,080
This shot...

201
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:39,840
What's the pose?

202
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,000
Smelling the flowers.

203
00:05:41,402 --> 00:05:41,960
(Hooked on taking photos)

204
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,280
Right.

205
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:43,920
Come on.

206
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,200
(Elderly people's photo pose 2: Smelling flowers)
Take this one.

207
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:46,920
Take this.

208
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:48,840
(Layering is the key)
We need to stagger our positions.

209
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:49,640
Right, just like this.

210
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,320
(Not enough photos yet)
Any other poses?

211
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:55,800
What else?

212
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,200
Walk touching the wall.

213
00:05:58,600 --> 00:05:59,400
Like this?

214
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,880
(Elderly people's photo pose 3:
Walking along the wall)

215
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:02,040
Right.

216
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:06,080
(Can't forget the scarf)
We need to have

217
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:07,760
one of these.

218
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:10,040
(Watch me show off)
Look, like this.

219
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:10,600
Look.

220
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,760
Ready? Go.

221
00:06:14,137 --> 00:06:15,954
(The scarf must flutter)

222
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,360
(Close contact with the wall again)
You'll scrape your palm.

223
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:20,160
Why take it so seriously?

224
00:06:21,240 --> 00:06:22,680
But the smelling flowers pose was great.

225
00:06:23,008 --> 00:06:23,560
(Still obsessed with smelling flowers)

226
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,360
I can also do this.

227
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:26,480
Any other poses?

228
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,400
You two can hold hands like this.

229
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,880
(Excited about this)
Come on.

230
00:06:30,680 --> 00:06:31,200
Like this.

231
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:32,480
Look up.

232
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:44,400
Pretty dizzying, right?

233
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:45,520
Like this?

234
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,120
Right, then freeze and smile.

235
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,200
Look over here. Look ahead.

236
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:49,720
(Standard smile)
Right.

237
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:53,040
Then lean your back a little.

238
00:06:53,179 --> 00:06:55,263
(Earth Group turns
into a senior tour group)

239
00:06:55,520 --> 00:06:56,600
Let's go quickly.

240
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:00,938
(What happened?)

241
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:02,000
(Just a moment ago)
This makes it simple.

242
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:02,680
Then let's do this.

243
00:07:02,798 --> 00:07:04,858
(Eavesdropping on intel)

244
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,440
Okay, we'll trade three for one.

245
00:07:07,917 --> 00:07:09,944
(Best intel-gathering spot secured)

246
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,720
(Unaware they're being overheard)
Fei arrived first, so it should be him.

247
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:19,400
No.

248
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,120
Who do you think, Xingxu?

249
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,880
I think it's Zhou Ye.

250
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:23,440
Okay, Zhou Ye, it is.

251
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:24,120
(They're actually guessing me?)

252
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:24,640
Really.

253
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,000
They say you're a guiding light.

254
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:28,400
Today we'll prove you're not.

255
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:30,600
You're a true master mind, okay?

256
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,200
Are you sure?

257
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:31,920
(Losing confidence)
Let me calculate again.

258
00:07:37,201 --> 00:07:39,920
(What are they doing?)

259
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,040
(Intel pouring in)
Let's not overthink it.

260
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:41,640
Okay.

261
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,400
Just run.

262
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,680
We three will trade ourselves for one.

263
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:45,240
Once done,

264
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,120
if the three of us
still haven't picked correctly,

265
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,760
then I'll surrender and admit defeat.

266
00:07:48,903 --> 00:07:51,158
(Seems like I overheard
something important)

267
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:52,080
Awesome.

268
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:52,920
Right?

269
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:54,000
To keep it simple.

270
00:07:54,080 --> 00:07:54,720
To keep it simple.

271
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:55,520
(Simplest is most direct)
We won't listen.

272
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,360
We use the simplest way.

273
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,280
It's a 75% chance.

274
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,680
If we don't get it right, so be it.

275
00:07:58,680 --> 00:07:59,160
Right.

276
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,240
Then we accept it.

277
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,840
If we're unlucky, what can we do?

278
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:02,520
We just pop.

279
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,484
(Straightforward charge)

280
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,000
Keep it simple.

281
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,320
This round,

282
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,840
(Let this be a warning)
we'll finish it within two minutes.

283
00:08:10,278 --> 00:08:12,213
(Need to slip away)

284
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,280
(Eavesdropping in vain)
Who on earth is it?

285
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,120
They just said

286
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:17,800
"Zhou Ye".

287
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,280
That's all I heard.

288
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:19,840
You and I were both mentioned.

289
00:08:20,400 --> 00:08:20,920
Look at us.

290
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:24,800
We scared them, right?

291
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,760
(Still absorbed in photo shooting)
We should reverse it like this.

292
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,440
Why don't we each just hold a balloon?

293
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:29,920
Hold hands.

294
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:31,040
That works too.

295
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:32,400
Ready?

296
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:33,200
Go.

297
00:08:34,037 --> 00:08:35,234
(Elderly people's photo pose +1)

298
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,120
Look at the expressions
of those two behind you.

299
00:08:37,264 --> 00:08:38,173
(Confused)

300
00:08:38,173 --> 00:08:38,964
(Puzzled)

301
00:08:39,316 --> 00:08:40,695
(Happy)

302
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:41,640
Just two kids.

303
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:45,800
When they arrive later,

304
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,120
we'll surround them.

305
00:08:47,172 --> 00:08:47,920
Come out!

306
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,040
Come out!

307
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,920
(Not sure who is surrounding whom)

308
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,000
Come over here!

309
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,120
You!

310
00:08:56,662 --> 00:08:58,244
- Come over here!
- Come over here!

311
00:08:59,323 --> 00:09:00,755
(Battle mode)

312
00:09:00,766 --> 00:09:03,320
(Carefree)

313
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,000
Three, two, one.

314
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:08,520
- Come over here!
- Come over here!

315
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:11,160
You guys started rehearsing?

316
00:09:11,977 --> 00:09:13,495
(Need to own that aura)

317
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,200
The "come over here" thing

318
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,560
looks pretty cool.

319
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:17,600
But the countdown part

320
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,520
(Pretty lame)
is pretty lame, you know?

321
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,440
You counted down three, two, one?

322
00:09:24,610 --> 00:09:25,230
(Aura)

323
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:27,120
These kids have it rough enough.

324
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:28,120
They're facing the light.

325
00:09:29,184 --> 00:09:30,760
(Too bright ahead)

326
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:34,120
(Heaven helps us)
You've lost based on positioning.

327
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:35,080
You're facing the light.

328
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:36,320
Let's talk in the alley.

329
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:38,640
No need.

330
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:42,920
Let's do it right now.

331
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,040
Me against Yuning.

332
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,760
Jingfei against Lin Yi.

333
00:09:45,880 --> 00:09:47,560
Why should we listen to you?

334
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:49,320
What do you want?

335
00:09:49,939 --> 00:09:51,158
(Tension is thick)

336
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:52,943
(Head-to-head clash)

337
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,360
Are you scared?

338
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:58,560
Yeah, we're scared.

339
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:01,600
We admit it.

340
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,720
(Outmatched, but loud and proud)

341
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:03,720
We're cowards.

342
00:10:04,120 --> 00:10:05,800
So come a bit closer.

343
00:10:05,896 --> 00:10:07,391
(Knowing when to fold)

344
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:09,200
Let's do this.

345
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:09,720
This round,

346
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,320
you pick one of us first,

347
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:16,080
and then we pick one of you.

348
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:16,800
How about that?

349
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,000
They step up
and pop each other's balloons.

350
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,040
(10 minutes ago)
We three will trade ourselves for one.

351
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:21,640
Once done,

352
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:23,520
if the three of us
still haven't picked correctly,

353
00:10:23,520 --> 00:10:24,400
then I'll surrender.

354
00:10:25,165 --> 00:10:25,520
(Just what I wanted)

355
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:26,320
Okay.

356
00:10:34,292 --> 00:10:36,002
(Just that confident)

357
00:10:36,002 --> 00:10:37,467
(A dashing silhouette)

358
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,120
It has started?

359
00:10:40,680 --> 00:10:42,000
That's too fast.

360
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:44,480
Is it you?

361
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:48,800
No, winning like this...

362
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,040
It's an unearned victory,

363
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:50,560
I think.

364
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:51,264
(The acting itch kicks in)

365
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:52,880
(Actor No. 2)
Yeah, this...

366
00:10:54,877 --> 00:10:55,832
(The fish took the bait)

367
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:57,040
Nothing unearned about it.

368
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,400
(Trying harder just hurts more)
If I picked wrong, then I lose.

369
00:11:00,124 --> 00:11:01,120
(Enjoying the show)

370
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:02,760
How is that unearned?

371
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,400
If I picked wrong, I lose,

372
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,520
and you're still alive.

373
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:06,640
(Speechless)
That's not the point.

374
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:08,920
Alright.

375
00:11:09,134 --> 00:11:10,040
(Speechless and secretly amused)

376
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,520
It's him, right?

377
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,960
(Victory is waving at us)
It's him.

378
00:11:14,120 --> 00:11:15,040
It's you.

379
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:15,560
It's him.

380
00:11:16,508 --> 00:11:17,737
(Getting deeper into character)

381
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,520
Wait, this is way too fast.

382
00:11:20,024 --> 00:11:21,701
(This is way too fun)

383
00:11:21,862 --> 00:11:24,320
(Can't hold it in)

384
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:24,720
Wait.

385
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,240
Then why...

386
00:11:25,240 --> 00:11:26,400
Why did you come over?

387
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:29,840
(A pro improvises with ease)
I wanted to scare him a bit.

388
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:30,800
Well, I didn't attack.

389
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,280
You came over to provoke me.

390
00:11:32,293 --> 00:11:33,736
(We got this in the bag)

391
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,920
Okay, come on, Yuning.

392
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:37,280
Give your balloon to Nai.

393
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:38,280
Hand it over.

394
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:42,960
You rushed it.

395
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,040
You lost it.

396
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:46,800
See? They panicked.

397
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,600
(Arrogant)
Why did you panic?

398
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:49,640
Does he still have a chance?

399
00:11:49,640 --> 00:11:50,720
Of course I do.

400
00:11:51,616 --> 00:11:52,985
(Look how smug he is)

401
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:58,400
Come on.

402
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:00,040
Come on.

403
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:00,480
Who?

404
00:12:01,182 --> 00:12:02,881
(Straight for the target)

405
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,000
But Fei was really hyped up,

406
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,240
so he might volunteer.

407
00:12:06,836 --> 00:12:08,054
(Took it to heart)

408
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,520
You need to think carefully.

409
00:12:11,040 --> 00:12:11,960
You can pop his.

410
00:12:15,225 --> 00:12:17,267
(Zero chill)

411
00:12:17,459 --> 00:12:18,240
(Watching the drama)

412
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,640
Go after him. What are you waiting for?

413
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,280
Go after him.

414
00:12:21,178 --> 00:12:22,119
(Flanked from both sides)

415
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:24,743
(Nowhere to run)

416
00:12:29,664 --> 00:12:31,043
(Cool and breezy)

417
00:12:32,411 --> 00:12:33,223
(Fell right for it)

418
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,880
Young people

419
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,440
are too impatient.

420
00:12:42,136 --> 00:12:43,825
(What is making him laugh so hard?)

421
00:12:43,825 --> 00:12:44,819
(One minute ago)

422
00:12:44,819 --> 00:12:46,113
(Totally immersed in the chase)

423
00:12:54,961 --> 00:12:56,180
(An intact balloon)

424
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:00,000
(Calm)
Give it back.

425
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:02,040
Why couldn't I pop it for so long?

426
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:05,000
I was squeezing this balloon for ages.

427
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
You fiddled with it?

428
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:09,800
That's hilarious.

429
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,320
Come on, Xingxu.

430
00:13:16,571 --> 00:13:17,328
(Got a bad feeling about this)

431
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,320
Give the balloon to Fei.

432
00:13:22,866 --> 00:13:24,074
(I feel you, bro)

433
00:13:24,074 --> 00:13:25,987
(Helpless)

434
00:13:28,787 --> 00:13:30,551
(Cocky)

435
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:40,200
Now your side sends someone
to challenge the other side.

436
00:13:47,212 --> 00:13:48,228
(Wang Yuwen enters the ring)

437
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:50,360
Come on.

438
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:52,440
Go for Yuwen.

439
00:13:54,256 --> 00:13:55,994
(Easily dodged)

440
00:13:56,265 --> 00:13:57,970
(Slowly approaching)

441
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,040
Strike now.

442
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:04,120
Wait.

443
00:14:07,198 --> 00:14:08,609
(Unable to help)

444
00:14:11,024 --> 00:14:12,157
(Heading in for backup)

445
00:14:13,643 --> 00:14:15,096
(Only dares to snatch the balloon)

446
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:17,320
Good.

447
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:22,040
You guys...

448
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:23,120
You couldn't help.

449
00:14:23,817 --> 00:14:25,217
(Utterly helpless)

450
00:14:27,804 --> 00:14:29,492
Their queen is Honglei.

451
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:31,680
Honglei.

452
00:14:31,801 --> 00:14:33,639
(Target locked)

453
00:14:33,799 --> 00:14:35,167
(How did he guess that?)

454
00:14:37,732 --> 00:14:39,100
(While everyone is brawling...)

455
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:41,131
(Slowly walking up)

456
00:14:41,986 --> 00:14:43,589
(Observing)

457
00:14:46,774 --> 00:14:48,195
(Watching from afar, afraid to engage)

458
00:14:48,640 --> 00:14:50,080
Honglei.

459
00:14:50,520 --> 00:14:51,760
So just go for Honglei.

460
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,440
Right?

461
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:55,960
Who was it just now?

462
00:14:55,960 --> 00:14:56,960
Me. I popped it.

463
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:57,440
You popped it?

464
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:58,480
Then step down.

465
00:14:58,840 --> 00:15:00,280
Nai, give the balloon to Yuwen.

466
00:15:06,621 --> 00:15:07,401
(Smug)

467
00:15:08,320 --> 00:15:09,840
Wait, what are you thinking?

468
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:11,640
Then you're out again.

469
00:15:11,640 --> 00:15:12,360
It's not her.

470
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,280
Give yours to her.

471
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,080
Give it to me.

472
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:15,520
Haven't we...

473
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:17,440
Haven't we already started the battle?

474
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:19,120
Yeah, but she isn't the queen.

475
00:15:19,120 --> 00:15:20,640
Then what does giving her
a new balloon mean?

476
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:21,800
I popped hers.

477
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:23,000
I'm eliminated.

478
00:15:25,440 --> 00:15:26,840
Stop arguing, guys.

479
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:28,626
(Weak and helpless)

480
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:29,840
Pop Lin Yi's.

481
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:31,680
Stop arguing, guys.

482
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:33,560
Guys, pop Lin Yi's.

483
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:35,040
(Your teammates are out)
Stop arguing, guys.

484
00:15:38,202 --> 00:15:39,966
(Ye hustling all on her own)

485
00:15:41,537 --> 00:15:42,349
(Spotted the stranded queen)

486
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:43,840
Honglei.

487
00:15:49,018 --> 00:15:50,240
(Stamina running low)

488
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,360
Out of these two, which one is yours?

489
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,040
Which one is yours?

490
00:15:52,737 --> 00:15:53,280
(No comment)

491
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:53,960
Alright then.

492
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:55,480
Then I'll wait here until you dry out,

493
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,280
Honglei.

494
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:59,280
Lin Yi is too tall.

495
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,080
He's too tall.

496
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:01,680
I can't do it.

497
00:16:01,832 --> 00:16:02,858
(Helping a teammate)

498
00:16:03,361 --> 00:16:05,028
(Defense mode)

499
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:10,800
Don't pop the wrong one.

500
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:20,040
It's boring.

501
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:21,120
Let's head back.

502
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,880
Let me tell you,

503
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:23,280
we've basically won this round.

504
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:26,280
In terms of stamina,
we'll definitely win.

505
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,920
Well, actually just now...

506
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:30,560
Lin Yi will wear himself out slowly.

507
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:32,160
Your side will wear out too.

508
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:32,480
It's the same.

509
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:33,080
It's the same.

510
00:16:33,211 --> 00:16:34,760
(Stuck in a deadlock)

511
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:36,920
Both teams now have
only two players left.

512
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:39,920
Both teams will discuss
whether to switch queens

513
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,080
and then make their final choice.

514
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:41,600
Okay.

515
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:44,080
Both teams have only
one chance to choose.

516
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:44,480
Right.

517
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:46,440
Popping the opponent's
queen balloon wins the game.

518
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,120
Exactly.

519
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:47,640
Okay.

520
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,680
Meeting time.

521
00:16:49,680 --> 00:16:51,040
Back to our losers' corner.

522
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,040
Meeting time.

523
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:53,520
Come on, let's go inside.

524
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:54,920
It's so tiring.

525
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:56,040
Stop talking.

526
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:56,435
(Emergency mute)

527
00:16:57,931 --> 00:16:59,427
(Same old strategy)

528
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,960
So, let's think

529
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:04,000
which of us shouldn't be the queen.

530
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,480
No, first guess if they'll switch.

531
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:05,797
(Start with the enemy first)

532
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:06,880
I don't think they'll switch.

533
00:17:07,119 --> 00:17:08,160
I don't think so either.

534
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,200
But we definitely need to switch.

535
00:17:10,319 --> 00:17:11,560
Will they think we'll switch?

536
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,720
I think they'll switch.

537
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,400
And they'll think we'll switch.

538
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,640
Then it's even.

539
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:18,839
So let's think one step ahead of them.

540
00:17:19,327 --> 00:17:21,518
(Brainstorming)

541
00:17:25,569 --> 00:17:26,787
(Totally clueless)

542
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:27,920
How about this?

543
00:17:28,480 --> 00:17:29,600
You play Zhou Ye,

544
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:30,760
and you play Honglei.

545
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:31,920
Let's run a simulation ourselves.

546
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,040
Okay, how do we simulate?

547
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:33,640
Tell us.

548
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:35,080
How can you simulate that?

549
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:35,840
(Curious)
I want to know.

550
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:36,360
You are Honglei,

551
00:17:36,360 --> 00:17:37,160
and you are Zhou Ye.

552
00:17:37,160 --> 00:17:38,920
(Director Lin online)
Use their mindset

553
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:40,600
to figure out whether we will switch.

554
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,040
Get into character now.

555
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:42,440
Right, get into character.

556
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:43,880
Okay, I'm channeling Honglei now.

557
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,120
You've already lost.

558
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:45,720
Okay, get into character.

559
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,440
We also need to figure out
who is the queen between you two.

560
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:47,840
Right.

561
00:17:52,127 --> 00:17:54,179
(Playing rock-paper-scissors)

562
00:17:54,179 --> 00:17:56,421
(Secret)

563
00:17:58,732 --> 00:18:00,440
(Spotting something)

564
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:01,240
What are they doing?

565
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:03,360
(They're eavesdropping)

566
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,610
(Let's fake it and fool them)

567
00:18:05,166 --> 00:18:06,384
(I get what you mean)

568
00:18:07,784 --> 00:18:09,270
(Completely unaware of being exposed)

569
00:18:09,933 --> 00:18:11,782
(Not a still image)

570
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:12,920
Come on, on three, two, one,

571
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:13,320
(Passionate acting begins)
We point together. Come on.

572
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,040
Okay.

573
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:15,520
Three, two, one.

574
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:24,440
(More and more invested)
Earlier we picked him and were wrong,

575
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:25,040
so now we pick you.

576
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:25,640
We pick Honglei.

577
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,480
Okay.

578
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:27,680
Okay.

579
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:28,880
You guys really figured this out.

580
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,360
(On an actor's professionalism)
Awesome. Brilliant.

581
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,040
I'm definitely winning.

582
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:34,080
That's how an actor should do it. Okay.

583
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:35,040
Directing, directing.

584
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:35,920
That's all that matters.

585
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:37,120
No problem.

586
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,400
Given what they said,

587
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:41,920
(Feeling something is off)
let's not act.

588
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,560
Let's play rock-paper-scissors.

589
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:44,840
(Using the same way to decide the queen)
Let's do the simplest way.

590
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:45,760
They deduced forever.

591
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:46,760
Come on, rock-paper-scissors.

592
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:47,120
Come on.

593
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:48,840
Rock, paper, scissors!

594
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,374
(Secret)

595
00:18:50,374 --> 00:18:53,720
(Which team will win in the end?)

596
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:54,840
You guys chatted so happily.

597
00:18:55,515 --> 00:18:56,040
(Full of confidence)

598
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:56,840
Come on.

599
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:58,040
The audience area is here.

600
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:58,520
